function strategyExplanation(){return `<details class="strategy-explanation"><summary>How the look-ahead works</summary><p>For each available player, we model your next two picks over 128 repeatable opponent draft orders. Opponents take players by ADP with independent normal variation: standard deviation = max(1.5 picks, ADP × uncertainty %). At 0%, they follow ADP exactly. This is an assumption, not a distribution measured from Underdog or DraftKings drafts.</p><p>We simulate opponents before your turn, take the candidate if available, then simulate opponents until your following turn. The best remaining player is selected using performance and the updated roster. Scores average only the scenarios where the candidate reaches your first turn. Low availability or fewer than 20 eligible scenarios means a fragile estimate.</p><p>Player value is adjusted FP/G in consensus mode. Imported-ranking mode uses 100 × (1 − (rank − 1) / highest source rank), a proxy with evenly spaced values. For Underdog, roster fit covers the weekly 2 G, 2 F, 1 C and 1 flex lineup. The bonus grows through the first six roster picks, prioritizing an uncovered required slot without rewarding endless depth at the same position. Flexible players fill only one slot.</p><p>“If you wait” estimates survival when you take the strongest immediate alternative instead. The common follow-up is the most frequently selected second player, not a promised pick. None or all of the sampled scenarios is displayed as &lt;1% or &gt;99%, never certainty.</p><p>Only undrafted players on your active board are modeled; ADP-only names absent from that board are excluded. Missing ADP substitutes board rank and makes estimates less reliable; a player without ADP has no displayed wait estimate. Unknown recorded picks or no ADP disable look-ahead. On your last roster pick, only immediate value matters. The model does not simulate opponent roster needs or a full draft.</p></details>`;}
function pickDetail(id){
 const a=analysis(state,room()),p=a.candidates.find(p=>p.id===id);if(!p)return;
 open('Why '+esc(p.name)+'?',`<p class="muted">${a.guidance.active?`Your picks ${a.myPick} and ${a.following} · ${a.guidance.between} opponent selections between turns`:'Immediate value · '+esc(a.guidance.reason)}</p><div class="table-scroll"><table class="comparison"><tbody><tr><th>Player value (${a.guidance.unit})</th><td>${num(p.baseValue)}</td></tr><tr><th>${a.guidance.bestBall?'Weekly lineup':'Roster'} bonus now</th><td>+${num(p.rosterBonus)}</td></tr><tr><th>Expected follow-up, including its roster bonus</th><td>${num(p.expectedNext)}</td></tr><tr><th>${a.guidance.active?'Expected two-pick score':'Pick score'}</th><td><b>${num(p.score)}</b></td></tr>${a.guidance.active?`<tr><th>Two-player value without roster bonuses</th><td>${num(p.pairProjection)}</td></tr><tr><th>Modeled availability at pick ${a.myPick}</th><td>${chance(p.myChance)} · ${p.samples} / ${a.guidance.scenarios} scenarios</td></tr><tr><th>Modeled survival to ${a.following} if you wait</th><td>${chance(p.waitChance)}</td></tr><tr><th>Common follow-up</th><td>${esc(p.nextPlayer||'None')} ${p.nextPlayer?'· '+chance(p.nextFrequency):''}</td></tr>`:''}</tbody></table></div>${a.guidance.active&&(p.samples<20||p.uncovered)?`<div class="notice">${p.samples<20?'Few scenarios reach your first turn with this player available. ':''}${p.uncovered?`${p.uncovered} eligible scenarios have no scored follow-up; those contribute zero second-pick value. Expand your projection coverage.`:''}</div>`:''}<p class="fineprint">ADP ${num(p.adp)} only influences opponent selections. Original source rank ${num(p.rank)}${room().orderMode==='consensus'?' · Consensus order '+num(p.consensusRank):''}. Scores do not change either order.</p>${strategyExplanation()}`,true);
}
